{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Many days.</b> Twenty-two years — from when he parted from him until Jacob went down to Egypt. For it is said: ״Joseph was seventeen years old,״ etc., and he was thirty years old when he stood before Pharaoh, and seven years of plenty, and two years of famine when Jacob came to Egypt — that makes twenty-two years, corresponding to the twenty-two years that Jacob did not fulfill the honor of father and mother (Megillah 16) — twenty years he was in Laban's house, and two years on the road upon returning from Laban's house; a year and a half in Sukkot and six months in Beth-El. And this is what he said to Laban: ״This is to me twenty years in your house״ — לי הן, עלי — and in the end I am flogged corresponding to them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:32.916641903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}